 ### [Exponential Approximation Method](2079-exponential-approximation-method.md)
-The Exponential Approximation Method (EAM) is a direct volume ray casting technique that approximates the continuous integral of light attenuation and emission along a ray using discrete steps and an exponential transmittance model. It differs from standard linear alpha compositing by scaling the sampled alpha values by a step-size-dependent correction factor, allowing for larger step sizes while maintaining visual fidelity to the exponential decay of light. It is typically chosen when performance is prioritized over exact physical accuracy, or when the volume data is sparse enough that early ray termination provides significant speedup.
